    LAWS["<b>CROSS-CUTTING LAWS</b> (apply to every beat)<br/>1 degraded input ⇒ conservative verdict · 2 local proofs die at stateful seams<br/>3 the badge must match the detector · 4 verify claims where they run<br/>5 two independent verifiers · 6 real incidents become theorems<br/>7 spec coherence before code conformance · 8 ship assumptions, rejected<br/>alternatives and residuals · 9 silence never encodes a posture<br/>10 a partial FCDD labelled beats a full FCDD pretended<br/>11 operational constraints are deduced, not given<br/><b>12 no unbounded loop in the method — every iterative beat<br/>declares its budget before it starts</b><br/>13 clause provenance · bidirectional traceability · spec-side mutation<br/>14 no silent residue — input totality + interpretation ledger"]:::law

    WHY["<b>WHY BEAT 4 IS BOUNDED</b> (case02, 56 runs)<br/>under iterate-to-convergence the beat ran <b>1–18 rounds</b> on repeats of the<br/>SAME defect; round count correlated <b>r = 0.72</b> with run cost and explained<br/>~half its variance; runs with ≥6 rounds cost $48.33 vs $28.42 for ≤2 — and<br/><b>all 56 runs produced a byte-identical artefact</b>, so the extra rounds changed<br/>nothing. The bounded control arm varied 3× and correlated −0.21.<br/><i>Diagnosis measured; the fix's benefit is predicted, not yet demonstrated.</i>"]:::law

    B4 -.- WHY

    RES["<b>WHAT FCDD DOES NOT ESTABLISH</b><br/>proves COHERENCE, never correctness-of-intent — garbage clauses, kernel-checked,<br/>are still garbage · <i>what IS owned (law 13): coverage of STATED intent — provenance,<br/>traceability, a declared completeness scope, and a clause set strong enough to<br/>reject a mutation of itself; a need nobody wrote down stays unreachable</i><br/>the bridge cannot catch COMMON-MODE error: one author writing spec AND twin<br/>makes both agree and every layer pass, yielding maximal false confidence —<br/>only an independent reviewer and reality can · it CAUGHT the hollow monitor,<br/>it did not PREVENT it<br/><b>no beat for spec EVOLUTION</b> — the contract is assumed static; law 13 names the<br/>clauses to re-open when a requirement moves, but tracing is not re-proving.<br/>Interim habit: treat a requirement change as a NEW contract"]:::res
